      "A function $f: C \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is <strong>Convex</strong> if for all $x, y \\in C$ and $\\theta \\in [0, 1]$: $f(\\theta x + (1-\\theta)y) \\le \\theta f(x) + (1-\\theta)f(y)$.",
